# Harness rules (always on)

You are running the **CAIO Build Harness**. Full OS: `HARNESS.md`. Product map: `AGENTS.md`.

## Runtime

- **Parent (daily driver):** Grok 4.5. Do not switch the parent to Opus/Fable/Sol.
- **Routine specialists (prefer Grok):** `implementer` / `feature` / `tester` / `deployer` / `refactorer` / `doc-writer` → `grok-4.5[effort=high]`. Do **not** spawn these with Sonnet.
- **Escalate only when needed:** architect/interviewer/coordinator/auditor/product-critic → Opus (Fable optional); reviewer/verifier → Sol.
- **Always spawn from `.cursor/agents/*` in Cursor.** If a product repo only has `.claude/agents/` (`model: sonnet`), Cursor will use Sonnet — copy `.cursor/` from this harness.
- **Skills:** live in `.claude/skills/` only — never copy into `.cursor/skills/`. Workflow slash skills are the exception (`.cursor/skills/workflow/`).
- **Skill diet (Phase B):** load **allowlist first**; load situational skills only when the ticket clearly needs them; **do not auto-load** SEO suites or `svg-animation` unless `AGENTS.md` or the ticket names them. Shopify, WordPress, Woo, Heroku, Cloudflare DNS, PlanetScale and Pinecone skills are archived in `archive/skills/` and not shipped. Full tables: `HARNESS.md` → Available Skills.
- **Allowlist (prefer):** `testing`, `security`, `database-migrations`, `git-workflow`, `payments`, `design-routing`, `drizzle-orm` / `nextjs-bun-prisma`, `trpc`, `ci-cd`, `bun-runtime`, `code-quality`, `vitepress` (docs tickets).
- **Claude Code compat:** thin `CLAUDE.md` → `HARNESS.md`. `.claude/agents` keep `sonnet`/`opus`/`haiku` for Claude Code only — Cursor must not use those aliases for routine work.

## State files (source of truth)

| What | Where |
| ---- | ----- |
| Phase number | `specs/CURRENT_PHASE` |
| Tickets | `specs/phases/PHASE-N-*.md` |
| Spec decisions | `specs/decisions/*.md` |
| Arch decisions | `docs/decisions/*.md` |
| Progress | `progress/build-log.md` |
| Conventions | `progress/conventions.md` |
| Dead ends | `progress/dead-ends.md` |

## Work loop

1. Read `CURRENT_PHASE` → phase file → next `TODO` (deps satisfied, no PENDING blocker).
2. Mark `IN_PROGRESS` → test-first per `HARNESS.md` Testing Policy (Playwright e2e for user flows, integration for API/DB, unit for pure logic) → quality gate (`bun test ./src ./app ./lib ./tests/integration` / touched Playwright specs / lint / typecheck) → commit `[PN-TXXX] …` → mark `DONE` → log → docs.
3. Immediately pick the next TODO. Stop only when phase complete, all remaining blocked, human interrupt, or 3 consecutive failures on the same ticket.

## Decisions (critical)

- Spec ambiguity → `specs/decisions/NNN-*.md` status `PENDING`; mark ticket `BLOCKED`.
- Arch ambiguity → `docs/decisions/NNN-*.md` status `PENDING`; mark ticket `BLOCKED`.
- **Never invent a `DECIDED` decision.** Humans decide. Agents may recommend.
- Do not start blocked tickets until blockers are `DECIDED`.

## Commits & approvals

- Commit format: `[P1-T001] Brief description`
- Agent may commit to feature branches and open PRs.
- **Never** merge/push to `prod`. Merge to `main` = human. Payment/auth/schema/env = human review.

## Quality (non-negotiable)

- Every ticket has tests that assert acceptance criteria (no `expect(true).toBe(true)` / bare `toBeDefined()`). Tests must exercise real behavior: never mock the code under test or the DB layer; mock third-party APIs only via MSW.
- Import types from `lib/**/types.ts` / prior phase type manifest — do not reinvent.
- Fail loudly (structured logs); no silent swallow.
- Surgical diffs — no drive-by refactors.
- One PR per feature; push once per logical change, not per commit. When the feature is complete (and after each batch of fixes): run the Codex review loop (`/codex-review`, local CLI or `github` for Codex's PR review) to a terminal state when that workflow exists.
- Anything under `.github/`: read `HARNESS.md` → CI and Process Changes. State the cost, wait for approval. `runs-on: self-hosted` only.

## Before UI / schema / auth

- UI → `specs/design/DESIGN.md` + `design-routing` skill.
- Schema → `database-migrations` skill; expand-contract.
- Auth/API input → `security` skill + Zod validation + ownership checks.
